This repository's "Releases" section provides a cache of s390x RPMs needed to
produce a devkit that is suitable for building the Red Hat Build of OpenJDK.

s390x requires special handling because the CentOS project never published
CentOS 7 binaries for s390x.  As a workaround, the devkit build logic --
currently residing in downstream patches to the Red Hat Build of OpenJDK sources
-- downloads the s390x binary RPMs from this repository's release section.  The
precise URLs are used in this repository's Makefile.

The s390x binary RPMs were built in IBM infrastructure (which has access to RHEL
7 s390x yum repositories) from the source RPMs downloaded by this repository's
Makefile, with the following mock invocations:

mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild alsa-lib-1.1.8-1.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild compat-glibc-2.12-4.el7.centos.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild cups-1.6.3-40.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild cups-1.6.3-51.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild fontconfig-2.13.0-4.3.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild freetype-2.8-14.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild gcc-4.8.5-39.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild gcc-4.8.5-44.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild genwqe-tools-4.0.20-3.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild glibc-2.17-292.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild glibc-2.17-317.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild kernel-3.10.0-1062.4.1.el7.src.rpm
mock --root rhel-7-s390x --rebuild kernel-3.10.0-1160.el7.src.rpm
